{"type": "term", "isPrimary": true, "textProcessorRuleChainCandidates": [[]], "inflectionRuleChainCandidates": [{"source": "algorithm", "inflectionRules": []}], "score": 0, "frequencyOrder": 0, "dictionaryIndex": 1, "dictionaryAlias": "", "sourceTermExactMatchCount": 1, "matchPrimaryReading": false, "maxOriginalTextLength": 4, "headwords": [{"index": 0, "headwordIndex": 0, "term": "bank", "reading": "bank", "sources": [{"originalText": "bank", "transformedText": "bank", "deinflectedText": "bank", "matchType": "exact", "matchSource": "term", "isPrimary": true}], "tags": [], "wordClasses": ["n", "v"]}], "definitions": [{"index": 0, "headwordIndices": [0], "dictionary": "New Oxford American Dict Yomi-v3", "dictionaryIndex": 1, "dictionaryAlias": "New Oxford American Dict Yomi-v3", "id": 1748700, "score": 0, "frequencyOrder": 0, "sequences": [0], "isPrimary": true, "tags": [], "entries": ["bank2  | baNGkb\u00e6\u014bk |\nnoun\na financial establishment that invests money deposited by customers, pays it\nout when required, makes loans at interest, and exchanges currency:  I paid\nthe money straight into my bank.\n\u2022 a stock of something available for use when required:  a blood bank |\nbuilding a bank of test items is the responsibility of teachers.\n\u2022 a site or receptacle where something may be stored:  the computer's memory\nbank.\n\u2022 a site or receptacle where something may be deposited for recycling:  a\npaper bank.\n\u2022 (the bank) the store of money or tokens held by the banker in some gambling\nor board games.\n\u2022 the person holding the store of money or tokens in a game; the banker.\n\u2022 US informal a large amount of money:  those entrepreneurs are raking in some\nserious bank |  the estate makes bank off the sale of merchandise.\nverb [with object]\ndeposit (money or valuables) in a bank:  I banked the check.\n\u2022 [no object] have an account at a particular bank:  he did not bank with the\nold family banks |  I\u2019ve banked at the same bank for nearly 50 years.\n\u2022 informal (especially of a competitor in a game or race) win or earn (a sum\nof money):  he banked $100,000 for a hole-in-one.\n\u2022 store (something, especially blood, tissue, or sperm) for future use:  the\nsperm is banked or held in storage for the following spring.\nPHRASES\nbreak the bank\n(in gambling) win more money than is held by the bank:  winning the pools was\nthe equivalent of breaking the bank at Monte Carlo.\n\u2022 [usually with negative] informal cost more than one can afford:  Christmas\nneed not break the bank.\nPHRASAL VERBS\nbank on\n(bank on something) base one's hopes or confidence on something:  they can\nbank on my winning 25 games next year.\nORIGIN\nlate 15th century  (originally denoting a money dealer's table): from French\nbanque  or Italian banca, from medieval Latin banca, bancus, of Germanic\norigin; related to bank1  and bench."]}, {"index": 1, "headwordIndices": [0], "dictionary": "kty-en-en", "dictionaryIndex": 2, "dictionaryAlias": "kty-en-en", "id": 2004004, "score": 0, "frequencyOrder": 0, "sequences": [0], "isPrimary": true, "tags": [{"name": "n", "category": "partOfSpeech", "order": -1, "score": 1, "content": ["noun"], "dictionaries": ["kty-en-en"], "redundant": false}], "entries": [{"type": "structured-content", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "preamble"}, "content": [{"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-Grammar"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "Grammar"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "Grammar-content"}, "content": "bank (countable and uncountable, plural banks)"}]}, {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-Etymology"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "Etymology"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "Etymology-content"}, "content": "Etymology tree\nProto-Indo-European *b\u02b0eg-der.\nProto-Germanic *bankiz\nProto-West Germanic *banki\nLombardic bankbor.\nItalian bancabor.\nMiddle French banqueder.\nEnglish bank\nFrom Middle English banke, from Middle French banque, from Italian banca (\u201ccounter, moneychanger's bench or table\u201d), from Lombardic bank (\u201cbench, counter\u201d), from Proto-West Germanic *banki, from Proto-Germanic *bankiz (\u201cbench, counter\u201d), from Proto-Indo-European *b\u02b0eg- (\u201cto turn, curve, bend, bow\u201d). Doublet of bench, banc, and banco.\nFor the bench-bank relation, compare typologically Russian \u043b\u0430\u0301\u0432\u043a\u0430 (l\u00e1vka), \u043f\u0440\u0438\u043b\u0430\u0301\u0432\u043e\u043a (pril\u00e1vok)."}]}]}]}, {"tag": "ol", "data": {"content": "glosses"}, "content": [{"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "An institution where one can place and borrow money and take care of financial affairs."]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "A branch office of such an institution."]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "An underwriter or controller of a card game."]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "A fund from deposits or contributions, to be used in transacting business; a joint stock or capital.", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-examples"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "1 example"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "Let it be no bank or common stock, but every man be master of his own money."}]}}]}]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "(gambling) The sum of money etc. which the dealer or banker has as a fund from which to draw stakes and pay losses."]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "sl", "title": "slang", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}, {"tag": "span", "content": "uncount", "title": "uncountable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "Money; profit.", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-examples"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "1 example"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "Military dude was working for a drug dealer, right? and making good bank with it\u2014he was making good money."}]}}]}]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "In certain games, such as dominos, a fund of pieces from which the players are allowed to draw."]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "(chiefly in combination) A safe and guaranteed place of storage for and retrieval of important items or goods.", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-examples"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "1 example"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "blood bank; data bank; sperm bank"}]}}]}]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "count", "title": "countable", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "A device used to store coins or currency.", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-examples"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "1 example"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "If you want to buy a bicycle, you need to put the money in your piggy bank."}]}}]}]}]}]}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "backlink"}, "content": [{"tag": "a", "href": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bank#English", "content": "Wiktionary"}]}]}]}, {"index": 2, "headwordIndices": [0], "dictionary": "kty-en-en", "dictionaryIndex": 2, "dictionaryAlias": "kty-en-en", "id": 2004005, "score": 0, "frequencyOrder": 0, "sequences": [0], "isPrimary": true, "tags": [{"name": "n", "category": "partOfSpeech", "order": -1, "score": 1, "content": ["noun"], "dictionaries": ["kty-en-en"], "redundant": true}], "entries": [{"type": "structured-content", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "preamble"}, "content": [{"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-Grammar"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "Grammar"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "Grammar-content"}, "content": "bank (plural banks)"}]}, {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-Etymology"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "Etymology"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "Etymology-content"}, "content": "From Middle English bank, banke, from Old English *banca (\u201cbench\u201d) (attested in Old English h\u014dbanca (\u201ccouch\u201d) and Old English banc (\u201cbank, hillock, embankment\u201d), from Proto-West Germanic *bank\u014d, from Proto-Germanic *bank\u00f4. Akin to Old Norse bakki (\u201celevation, hill\u201d), Norwegian bakke (\u201cslope, hill\u201d)."}]}]}]}, {"tag": "ol", "data": {"content": "glosses"}, "content": [{"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": ["(hydrology) An edge of river, lake, or other watercourse.", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content": "details-entry-examples"}, "content": [{"tag": "summary", "data": {"content": "summary-entry"}, "content": "2 examples"}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "Tiber trembled underneath her banks."}]}}, {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "extra-info"}, "content": {"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence"}, "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "example-sentence-a"}, "content": "On the opposite bank of the river other Chinese units attacked Taoshih and Yunmeng north-west of Hankow."}]}}]}]}]}, {"tag": "li", "content": [{"tag": "div", "content": [{"tag": "div", "data": {"content": "tags"}, "content": [{"tag": "span", "content": "\ud83d\udea2", "title": "nautical", "data": {"content": "tag", "category": ""}}]}, "(hydrology) An elevation under the sea; a shallow area of shifting sand, gravel, mud, and so forth", {"tag": "details", "data": {"content"